1
00:01:33,039 --> 00:01:38,259
[First Love Again]

2
00:01:38,460 --> 00:01:40,900
[Episode 13]

3
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:30,900
Miss.

4
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:33,150
Have a taste. They're fresh. Just came in.

5
00:02:33,150 --> 00:02:33,750
No, no, no.

6
00:02:33,750 --> 00:02:34,840
That's okay, thank you.

7
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:35,710
Miss, miss.

8
00:02:35,710 --> 00:02:37,960
Give it a try. They're really fresh.

9
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:38,710
I...

10
00:02:41,630 --> 00:02:43,750
Go on, try a piece. They're really sweet.

11
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:45,150
Look, so fresh.

12
00:02:45,150 --> 00:02:46,610
Just arrived. Take a look.

13
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,870
So sweet, so sweet.

14
00:02:57,079 --> 00:02:58,079
But aren't lemons

15
00:02:58,100 --> 00:02:59,230
supposed to be sour?

16
00:03:01,630 --> 00:03:02,240
Like this?

17
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:02,910
Here, let me help you.

18
00:03:02,910 --> 00:03:04,360
-Okay.
-I think so...

19
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:04,710
Right.

20
00:03:04,710 --> 00:03:05,800
-It's upside down.
-It's upside down.

21
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:06,460
Over there.

22
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:14,360
Someone's bad-mouthing us, right?

23
00:03:14,430 --> 00:03:15,840
Must be those two.

24
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:18,360
Do you think they'll both bail

25
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:19,280
once they see each other?

26
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,310
No.

27
00:03:20,310 --> 00:03:22,240
We specifically asked them
to buy so many things.

28
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,120
One person can't carry them all.

29
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,710
They'll have to come together.

30
00:03:24,710 --> 00:03:26,590
Does this count as
"inviting them into the urn"?

31
00:03:26,590 --> 00:03:29,079
That's for
when you pay someone back in kind,

32
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:30,030
dummy.

33
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:34,310
It's just a rental.
Do we really need to do all this?

34
00:03:34,310 --> 00:03:35,640
This must've cost a lot.

35
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:36,630
Of course we have to!

36
00:03:36,630 --> 00:03:40,630
Even when you're renting, you've got to
care about your quality of life.

37
00:03:45,190 --> 00:03:46,030
Hurry up.

38
00:03:46,030 --> 00:03:48,490
We still have to
put all the bedding on later.

39
00:03:58,079 --> 00:03:59,960
Avocado flavor...

40
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:16,430
[Li Sirui] [Avocado-flavored potato chips]

41
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:48,750
[Paper Goods]

42
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:58,760
[Paper Goods]

43
00:05:17,470 --> 00:05:18,700
[Shopping List] [Menstrual Pads]

44
00:05:50,270 --> 00:05:51,670
Are you looking for this?

45
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:07,310
Weren't you out of town?

46
00:06:09,070 --> 00:06:10,070
"Out of town"?

47
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:16,480
Li Sirui is having
a housewarming party today.

48
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:18,610
He asked me to help him buy some things.

49
00:06:22,550 --> 00:06:24,440
[Le Xiaotao]

50
00:06:27,030 --> 00:06:28,380
[Li Sirui]

51
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:06,830
Thank you.

52
00:07:06,830 --> 00:07:07,760
You're welcome.

53
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:16,220
Let's go together.

54
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:30,390
Coming.

55
00:07:30,430 --> 00:07:31,310
Wow, that's a lot of stuff.

56
00:07:31,310 --> 00:07:32,120
-Come on in.
-Xiangxiang, you're here.

57
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,120
No need to take off your shoes. It's fine.

58
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:33,870
Here, let me take those.

59
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:34,730
-Welcome.
-Hi.

60
00:07:34,950 --> 00:07:35,600
Hi.

61
00:07:36,390 --> 00:07:37,830
You bought so much.

62
00:07:38,190 --> 00:07:40,270
Didn't you say Gu Han went out of town?

63
00:07:41,310 --> 00:07:42,000
Out of town...

64
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,560
Yeah. Anywhere off campus counts as

65
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:44,890
out of town, doesn't it?

66
00:07:45,830 --> 00:07:46,720
Oh, Xiangxiang.

67
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:48,270
-Did you get everything?
-We're craving some spicy shrimp.

68
00:07:48,270 --> 00:07:49,360
-Go make it for us.
-Yeah.

69
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,620
We're counting on you.

70
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:51,600
It's all here.

71
00:07:59,070 --> 00:08:00,720
Alright, leave this to us.

72
00:08:00,830 --> 00:08:02,290
Go help out in the kitchen.

73
00:08:03,390 --> 00:08:04,040
Go.

74
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:16,960
Anything I can help with?

75
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:20,060
You wash the vegetables,
and I'll chop them.

76
00:08:33,789 --> 00:08:34,590
What's wrong?

77
00:08:34,789 --> 00:08:36,030
I don't know what's been going on lately.

78
00:08:36,030 --> 00:08:37,270
I've been getting a lot of haters,

79
00:08:37,270 --> 00:08:39,530
and their comments are getting nastier.

80
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:41,270
But look,

81
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:42,750
there's this one fan
who's really got my back.

82
00:08:42,429 --> 00:08:43,240
[Scammer! Used it and my face got ruined!
The streaming industry needs cleaning up!]

83
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:44,550
They clap back
at every hateful comment for me.

84
00:08:43,270 --> 00:08:44,179
[This streamer ruined me! Scammer!
Give me my money back, now!]

85
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:45,750
I've been streaming for so long,

86
00:08:45,750 --> 00:08:47,750
and I've never seen such a great fan.

87
00:08:56,670 --> 00:08:57,440
Thank you.

88
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,840
Friends, thank you for coming today.

89
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:29,510
Actually, the main purpose
of this housewarming party

90
00:09:29,510 --> 00:09:30,670
is to...

91
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,840
officially announce
that Xiaotao and I are together.

92
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:37,320
From now on, we'll be a perfect pair,

93
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,390
carrying on in secret.

94
00:09:38,390 --> 00:09:40,080
I toil away, and she tends the home.

95
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,840
Please give us a round of applause.

96
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:43,240
That's not how you say it.

97
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:45,870
You're a Chinese major, and your boyfriend
is misusing idioms like that.

98
00:09:45,870 --> 00:09:47,390
Aren't you going to do something
about him?

99
00:09:47,390 --> 00:09:48,030
Alright.

100
00:09:48,030 --> 00:09:49,630
We've had enough gossip. Let's eat.

101
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:50,440
Yes, eat more.

102
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:51,120
From now on, this place will be

103
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,510
our usual hangout spot.

104
00:09:53,030 --> 00:09:53,720
Wait.

105
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:55,840
We should toast
Xiangxiang and Gu Han first.

106
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,200
Thank you for preparing
such a hearty dinner

107
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:58,120
for us today.

108
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:58,960
Thank you.

109
00:09:59,030 --> 00:09:59,600
-Come on.
-Cheers.

110
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,000
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

111
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,550
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

112
00:10:06,150 --> 00:10:07,200
These are the shrimp Xiangxiang made.

113
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:08,200
You must try them.

114
00:10:09,030 --> 00:10:10,630
Come on, try some.

115
00:10:10,790 --> 00:10:12,630
-Come on, Xiangxiang.
-These must be delicious.

116
00:10:12,630 --> 00:10:13,200
Thank you.

117
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:14,080
Help yourself.

118
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:15,630
Thank you.

119
00:10:19,210 --> 00:10:20,280
-The shrimp Xiangxiang made.
-Help yourself.

120
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:21,140
That's enough.

121
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:22,420
I'll get it myself.

122
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,720
Since we're almost done eating,

123
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:33,840
let's play a game.

124
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:34,290
Sure.

125
00:10:34,310 --> 00:10:34,840
Okay.

126
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,790
Then let's play a party game.

127
00:10:36,810 --> 00:10:38,910
Whoever the bottle points to
has to play Truth or Dare. How about that?

128
00:10:38,910 --> 00:10:39,510
-Okay.
-Sure.

129
00:10:39,510 --> 00:10:41,170
We can't play this game
without a lie detector.

130
00:10:41,170 --> 00:10:43,430
-I'll go get it. You guys clean up.
-Okay.

131
00:10:47,030 --> 00:10:48,560
Come on, who's going first?

132
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:51,000
-You spin the bottle.
-I'll spin it.

133
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:51,630
Here we go.

134
00:10:51,790 --> 00:10:54,120
One, two, three.

135
00:10:55,630 --> 00:10:56,960
Xiangxiang!

136
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:58,670
-You'll definitely choose Truth, right?
-I...

137
00:10:58,670 --> 00:10:59,550
Come on.

138
00:11:00,790 --> 00:11:01,720
I'll ask.

139
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:04,000
Among all the guys here,

140
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,400
